  "details": "Heya! soooo, i've seen maybe a few posts regarding the addition of a book reading feature into vrchat.\n\nim sure its possible as i've seen much heftier systems added as features recently added into vrchat.\n\ni understand that it would be a niche audience that this feature would relate to, but it would still be a great and interesting feature nonetheless.\n\ni was thinking maybe partnering with Webtoon and Audible to get webcomics and audiobooks added as a alternative to actual books. maybe partnering with a free library that is willing to share its digital contents with the users of vrchat.\n\nnow obviously it would be difficult to get any attention brought to this and make it worthwhile to add into vrchat without monetization to cover potential costs when partnering with audible and webtoon. so i propose that this is a paid feature and it be locked behind VRC+ so we are technically paying for a subscription to the book service as well.\n\nalso, would it be possible to add both a book with interactable pages AND and E-Reader option to make it less complicated to turn pages for desktop users.",
